/// Chapter 48 of the guide, written from md-docs/48-contributing.md by
/// scripts/site-from-guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page ContributingGuide(path: "/docs/guide/contributing", title: "Contributing", description: "The repository, the compiler pipeline, building and testing, changing a built-in, the grammar or the runtime, and the guide's checks.", layout: DocsShell("Contributing", chapter: t("guide.chapter", { n: "48" }), blurb: "How the compiler is put together, how to build and test it, and how to change the language, a built-in or this guide.", source: "md-docs/48-contributing.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "the-repository", label: "The repository"), Anchor(id: "the-pipeline", label: "The pipeline"), Anchor(id: "building-and-testing", label: "Building and testing"), Anchor(id: "changing-things", label: "Changing things"), Anchor(id: "the-guide", label: "The guide"), Anchor(id: "releasing", label: "Releasing")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/glossary", prevLabel: "47. {t("ch.47")}")) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("WebFluent is one Rust crate — the compiler and the `wf` binary — with a language server beside it, editor extensions, a small JavaScript runtime and this guide, all in one repository: [github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent](https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent).")

        Heading("The repository", id: "the-repository").h2

        CodeBlock(#"src/
  lexer/, parser/, syntax/   source → tokens → tree; the .wfx layout in layout/
  sema/                      semantic checks, and the type checker (types.rs)
  linter/                    accessibility, contrast, unused, vocabulary, PDF and slide rules
  registry/                  every built-in's props, cases, flags, events, slots, parts
  codegen/                   JavaScript, HTML, CSS, the static paint, SEO, the service worker
  runtime/modules/           the browser runtime, one file per module
  themes/                    the baseline tokens and the built-ins' CSS
  template/                  the template engine behind `wf render`
  media/                     the image pipeline
  cli/                       each `wf` command
crates/wf-lsp/               the language server
editors/                     VS Code, Zed and the Tree-sitter grammars
md-docs/                     this guide
site/                        the documentation site, written in WebFluent
tests/                       Rust integration tests, tests/js (runtime), tests/browser (Chrome)
spec/                        design notes and plans"#, title: "text")

        Heading("The pipeline", id: "the-pipeline").h2

        CodeBlock(#".wf / .wfx → lexer → parser → lower → semantic checks → type checker → linters → code generators
                                                                                 ├─ JavaScript + HTML + CSS
                                                                                 └─ PDF / slides"#, title: "text")

        Markdown("Every stage reads the **registry** for what a built-in takes, so a prop added there is known to the checker, the linters, the language server, `wf docs` and the [components reference](/docs/reference) at once.")

        Heading("Building and testing", id: "building-and-testing").h2

        Terminal(lines: [
                Line(command: "cargo build"),
                Line(command: "cargo test --workspace"),
                Line(command: "node --test tests/js/*.test.mjs"),
                Line(command: "cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings")
            ])

        Markdown("The browser suites need Chrome: `cd tests/browser && npm ci && node offline.mjs` (and `peer.mjs`). CI runs all of it on every push.")

        Heading("Changing things", id: "changing-things").h2

        Markdown("- **A built-in's props or flags**: edit `src/registry/builtins.rs`, its CSS in `src/themes/`, and its code generation; then run `python3 scripts/components-reference.py` to rewrite the reference.\n- **The grammar**: the parser in `src/parser/v2.rs`, the formatter and the `.wfx` layout, and both Tree-sitter grammars in `editors/`. The guide's own code blocks are the grammar's test corpus.\n- **The runtime**: a module in `src/runtime/modules/`; the manifest that says what reaches it is rewritten by a Rust test. Add a test in `tests/js/`.\n- **A diagnostic**: give it a code, an entry with a failing example in [Diagnostics](/docs/guide/diagnostics) — the test suite compiles every example and checks it draws its code.")

        Heading("The guide", id: "the-guide").h2

        Markdown("The guide lives in `md-docs/`, one file per chapter, and is the source of the documentation site: `python3 scripts/site-from-guide.py` writes the site's chapter pages, sidebar and search index from it. Each chapter starts with a comment naming its route, its group in the sidebar, the line under its title and its search description.\n\nThe test suite holds the guide to the compiler:\n\n- every `wf` code block parses, type-checks and compiles without a warning;\n- every `wf expect CODE` block draws exactly that code;\n- every link between chapters, and every anchor, resolves;\n- every declaration, keyword, built-in, browser value, built-in function, config key, command and diagnostic code appears in it;\n- the tokens chapter is the baseline, and the configuration chapter's defaults are the compiler's;\n- the site's pages are what the generator writes from the guide.\n\nA code block that is deliberately incomplete says so with a `…`, and is only checked for spelling.")

        Heading("Releasing", id: "releasing").h2

        Markdown("[`RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/blob/master/RELEASING.md) in the repository has the steps: one tag builds the binaries, the packages and the editor extensions.")
    }
}
